      "text": "Nemotron 3.5 Parse is a compact vision-language model from NVIDIA designed to extract structured content from document page images, preserving reading order and assigning content categories for downstream use in retrieval-augmented generation (RAG) and autonomous agents. It is trained via supervised fine-tuning on document understanding tasks followed by reinforcement learning to improve extraction accuracy, consistency, and completion reliability. The model is optimized for efficient inference and can be further customized with synthetic data and speculator-based acceleration."
